{"title":"2024 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Verifying_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Verifying Solutions</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lauren plays basketball with her friends. She makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> baskets. Each of these baskets is worth either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points. Lauren scores a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points. How many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point baskets did she make?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/702c3473a41d6c73fbbf4a9c188ea0c864850bf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 6 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 7 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 8 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-point baskets that Lauren made and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-point baskets that she made. Using the information from the problem, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314a18c6b0fb2689e94987ee90b61b3fa94c755b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> (since she made <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> baskets in total)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/322073c7743033ccdb1b997f091d9fa7bf7a3974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 3y = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" /> (since the baskets gave <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points in total)\n</p><p>Multiplying the first equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/14439363569d24f5849b002f87fdfc0f6e85a6ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 2y = 10 \\times 2 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting this from the second equation involving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec3380e8bddbd3e8f3ef22a4c12c219fcd36b5fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 3y - 2x - 2y = 26 - 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"228\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/1617423c7c3f10ca79d25b4883cd87e48142581d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"91\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-point baskets in total that Lauren made. Since she made <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> baskets in total, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552f7934039e148cff4c1aedee0f06ba6940228d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> of those were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-point baskets.\n</p><p>Since all of the baskets Lauren made gave her <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points in total, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf7f26c2c4a0411c35087cac320ae57ceab92380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(10 - x) + 3x = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb9cb547d02cf5c94c61e0d8f48ca83fe3041e0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 10 - 2 \\times x + 3x = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"199\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aef4bc84b7ddee0a5e57599c8c2e740a3d2e23a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 20 = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef03c5193b5c5f9ffa3ef62753655f0ade2a18bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 26 - 20 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"174\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(answer_choices)\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-point baskets that Lauren made and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-point baskets that she made. Using the information from the problem, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314a18c6b0fb2689e94987ee90b61b3fa94c755b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/322073c7743033ccdb1b997f091d9fa7bf7a3974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 3y = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>From the second equation, we can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> is even because it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times some integer, so an even number must be added to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. However, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be even for the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be even.\n</p><p>This eliminates answers A, C, and E because they are odd numbers, meaning that they aren't divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Next, we can try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff8bbad79fc034a1b35329acef5492dc937ecd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff8bbad79fc034a1b35329acef5492dc937ecd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e25b01aa27f7a9bdd16f7e84aec03d83a9e283.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 3 \\times 8 = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d0a10c6dfc8a2584fa25178832c45fe1084a2c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 24 = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93fd552d6bc3014c997bc80cee1a252047b4e4b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 26 - 24 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bfb3f05ecef2d161db0a7f2ba90aea393ca6efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{2}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>However, we realize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/703f6be1b7d8f12fc60b9a3c5cb1876a65e775af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 1 + 8 = 9 \\neq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />. This eliminates answer choice D.\n</p><p>We could have also realized that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff8bbad79fc034a1b35329acef5492dc937ecd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a38af3643f2d8f8c648534414b162b193eae52e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 10 - 8 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82db1f57bc65a395b71a8992b032a0636dd7940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2 + 3 \\times 8 = 4 + 24 = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"221\" height=\"15\" />, which doesn't match with the total number of points that Lauren got.\n</p><p>Since all of the other answer choices have been eliminated, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/d/36d64af86d44c520fca5a26f234c81e4576609e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Verifying_Solutions\">Verifying Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Verifying Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the baskets that Lauren made were each worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, she would have had to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c895eaeac14cc5f479e005a559061e4fbd7dded0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - 6 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> baskets that were each worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points because she made <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> baskets in total.\n</p><p>If she had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> baskets each worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, those baskets would have given her <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/ddeeb0e9d55135dda490dab8ffe94420738085d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 3 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> points\n</p><p>If she had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> baskets each worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, those baskets would have given her <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037bd49957923de4c5fb6cac7257f72b4dc64a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> points.\n</p><p>In total, this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/50028d1c8057a5f0f5ebe964bfd574e7f75daed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 + 8 = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> points. Since this matches what she really got, we have verified our solution.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2024 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2024 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC